                    {
                        "form_id": "52ddfa5f-3fa8-4b01-8256-d256dc19865d",
                        "entry_id": "c0534ff5-1ef3-3909-a56a-92f879c6d2b3",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "fecked"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c823a3da-66a3-30cf-a38f-cb329ec8ad1e",
                        "entry_id": "c0534ff5-1ef3-3909-a56a-92f879c6d2b3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Used in place of fuck."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Ireland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec27612e-e5e1-4cbb-9ecd-6c305241543d",
                                "sense_id": "c823a3da-66a3-30cf-a38f-cb329ec8ad1e",
                                "text": "Earlier there was a dispute between the Chair and Proinsias de Rossa concerning the words used when a wife is getting rid of her husband. In the case of Deserted Wives' Allowance, Mr de Rossa said, it had to be proved that the wife didn't tell her husband to \"feck off\". Mr Tunney suggested that \"get lost\" might be a more appropriate expression for Mr de Rossa to use."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "97dc8995-9b14-4b50-b606-a289095f8c33",
                                "sense_id": "c823a3da-66a3-30cf-a38f-cb329ec8ad1e",
                                "text": "\"Why are you fecking around with this Family Planning Bill when people are dying?\" - Senator David Norris to the Minister for Health, Dr O'Connell, on the Bill which does not allow condoms to be sold from vending machines."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d58f1a2d-d6c1-4346-8ef2-0f58bd905da8",
                                "sense_id": "c823a3da-66a3-30cf-a38f-cb329ec8ad1e",
                                "text": "Father Jack Hackett: Tea? Feck! […] Mrs. Doyle: I'll tell you what, Father. I'll pour a cup for ye anyway and y' can have it if ya want. Now... And what do you say to a cup?\nFather Jack Hackett: Feck off, cup!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1967fa0-2216-4cef-b88a-f288f1d165a4",
                                "sense_id": "c823a3da-66a3-30cf-a38f-cb329ec8ad1e",
                                "text": "As Charlie Murphy put it to me, 'When the bishops called down fire and brimstone not a man stirred but when Joe Christle fecked off half the shagging IRA followed him!'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "728b9cba-42f5-4f53-b388-42fb71f5efec",
                                "sense_id": "c823a3da-66a3-30cf-a38f-cb329ec8ad1e",
                                "text": "It didn't stop him turning to a reporter, saying \"feck it\" and nipping out anyway to talk to friends."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "843f1310-d102-4aea-815c-d2ae4cdf960d",
                                "sense_id": "c823a3da-66a3-30cf-a38f-cb329ec8ad1e",
                                "text": "\"My family were Irish,\" she says, \"and the use of the word 'feck' was normal but, of course, as a child, I thought it was a swear word. My first day at Holycross I heard the nuns saying feckin' this and feckin' that and I thought, 'Oh my God, they're all swearing'[\"]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7c067e7-1516-427f-8dbd-04e86ac891c6",
                                "sense_id": "c823a3da-66a3-30cf-a38f-cb329ec8ad1e",
                                "text": "the year gets off to a flying start when the words 'Oh feck' are uttered collectively by two million as the January wage sheets are handed out and the true realisation of the Budget kicks in"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "493d3a61-8725-4e0e-bbfb-caf87083223e",
                                "sense_id": "c823a3da-66a3-30cf-a38f-cb329ec8ad1e",
                                "text": "And though she had no qualms of submitting to this bubbling desire coiling within her, for she was no prim virgin, she sensed far more than her body was going to get fecked."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db4c09ac-b6e4-4ebb-94e4-60b7b5517698",
                                "sense_id": "c823a3da-66a3-30cf-a38f-cb329ec8ad1e",
                                "text": "“I never thought the problem would be of this magnitude. I really didn’t think I’d be waking up this morning to this type of news,” an emotional Ms Phelan said, adding that “they fecked with the wrong women.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0144045d-3a77-42da-9b11-d46f3f3a0f2b",
                                "sense_id": "c823a3da-66a3-30cf-a38f-cb329ec8ad1e",
                                "text": "But if you’re not going to set your own trends, and work to your own team, you’re fecked."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
